WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.150
Viewers have found a lot to like about the
original series The Witcher, which stars erstwhile

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.950
Superman Henry Cavill as Geralt of Rivia,
the protagonist of the well-loved series of

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:10.760
video games.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.620
It's well-written, briskly paced, lovingly
rendered fantasy fun.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.660
And while some critics have tried to rain
on fans' parade, those fans have been quick

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.920
to write off these half-baked criticisms.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.880
Rightly so, in our humble opinion.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.940
A good number appear to have been fielded
by critics who either don't care for the fantasy

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:31.730
genre in general, or can't keep from comparing
The Witcher to the recently-ended Game of

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.220
Thrones, which is frankly a ridiculously weak
comparison.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.820
Cavill acquits himself nicely in the lead,
but viewers have been particularly taken with

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:44.480
the character of Yennefer, a sorceress with
a troubled history and decidedly mixed feelings

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.480
about Geralt.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.800
"Tell me, are there women who find this coarseness
charming?

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.640
Maybe someplace where they find your coin
very charming indeed."

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.220
The show-stealing magic user, who becomes
ever more powerful as the first season goes

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:03.210
on and eventually has occasion to use her
formidable powers to take on an entire army

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:08.390
single-handedly, is portrayed by young actress
Anya Chalotra, a relative newcomer whom you

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:10.780
might nevertheless find to be a bit familiar.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.580
If you can't quite put your finger on where
you've seen her before, well, we're here to

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.080
help.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.380
Chalotra hasn't been in the business for very
long, but her talent has already earned her

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.080
some pretty high-profile gigs.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.890
Since we'll assume you're a fan of The Witcher,
you obviously have a Netflix subscription,

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:30.870
meaning that you might have caught her debut
credit: 2018's Wanderlust, a drama series

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:34.000
which is a joint production between the streamer
and BBC One.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.940
The series stars Toni Collette as Joy Richards,
a therapist whose life goes into a downward

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.619
spiral after both the death of one of her
patients and a terrible car accident in which

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.780
she's badly injured.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:49.760
The series is the brainchild of British playwright
Nick Payne, who recently branched out into

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:55.009
feature film work with his screenplay for
the 2017 adaptation of Julian Barnes' novel

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:55.960
The Sense of an Ending.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.200
Its well-received first season introduced
Chalotra in a minor role, and gave her the

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.920
opportunity to work alongside the always-excellent
Collette, as well as co-stars Steven Mackintosh

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.000
and Zawe Ashton.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.080
While the series' first season left a number
of narrative threads dangling, there hasn't

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:15.250
yet been any word on whether a second has
received the official greenlight, let alone

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.820
whether Chalotra will return.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.900
Whether or not the young star is tapped for
another round of Wanderlust, though, it appears

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.840
likely she'll be kept plenty busy.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:29.080
Also in 2018, Chalotra appeared in the BBC
One miniseries The ABC Murders, an adaptation

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.600
of the classic Agatha Christie novel of the
same name.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:35.800
Once again, she had the privilege of working
with an outstanding cast, led by the great

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.920
John Malkovich as Hercule Poirot.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.940
The miniseries is available for streaming
in the U.S. on Amazon Prime Video.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.920
Interestingly, Chalotra has also shown an
early talent for voice acting.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:51.840
The only other credit on her resume: the YouTube
Premium animated series Sherwood, an ambitious,

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.160
futuristic adaptation of the Robin Hood legend
set in the 23rd century.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.740
Chalotra leads the series as the gender-swapped
Robin Loxley.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.880
Her co-stars include Tyler Posey, Jamie Chung,
Rachel House, and Joseph Fiennes.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.800
She may be a relatively new face, but with
credits this interesting, Chalotra has already

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:14.430
proven her versatility — and with The Witcher,
she's proven that she can win over fans and

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.020
hold her own against the charismatic likes
of Cavill.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:18.360
"What?

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.760
You were going to summon chaos on king's orders
between feeding and naps?"

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.100
"Do not patronize me."

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.720
We think it's safe to say that we'll be seeing
much, much more of her in the years to come.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.860
While her IMDb page doesn't currently list
any upcoming projects, we already know that

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:38.200
we'll be getting a second season of The Witcher,
as it was renewed by Netflix before the first

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.260
season even dropped.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.440
Given fans' warm response to the character
of Yennefer, we'd be surprised if Chalotra

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:46.360
weren't given an expanded role for the series'
second outing.

